# Cursor / AI assistant rules for Nomads Boys Hostel — Manager

## Stack
- React 19 + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind v4
- shadcn/ui (Radix primitives) + lucide-react icons
- Zustand for state, React Hook Form + Zod for forms
- Recharts for charts, Sonner for toasts, date-fns for dates
- jsPDF + xlsx for report exports

## Branch workflow — HARD RULE
- The default working branch is `feature/finance-section`. **Never commit to `main`.**
- Branch naming: `feature/<short>`, `fix/<short>`, `chore/<short>`, `experiment/<short>`.
- Push the feature branch to GitHub, never to `main`.
- Wait for explicit user instruction ("merge to main" / "deploy to main") before merging.
- Verify the deployed URL renders without errors before claiming work is done.

## Naming (USER-FACING TEXT)
- "Student" → "Nomad" (singular) / "Nomads" (plural)
- "Visitor" → "Guest" / "Guests"
- The TypeScript types are still `Student`, `Visitor` (and so are the
  route paths `/students`, `/visitors`, and the data fields `studentId`,
  `visitorId`). Don't rename those — too much blast radius, no UX benefit.

## UI conventions
- **Reuse existing primitives** — shadcn components in `src/components/ui/`.
  Don't pull in new UI libraries.
- **No gradients, glassmorphism, decorative illustrations, excessive animations.**
- **Design system**: Poppins (headings) + Inter (body); neutral palette with one
  dark accent. Soft pill badges.
- **PageHeader** is the standard top-of-page header (title + description +
  optional actions). The actions prop is a single ReactNode — wrap multiple
  buttons in a `<div className="flex items-center gap-2">`.
- **Form sheets** (`*Sheet.tsx`) use the shadcn Sheet primitive. Forms use
  react-hook-form + zod resolver, with `<FormField>` + `<FormItem>` +
  `<FormLabel>` (props `required` / `optional`) + `<FormControl>` +
  `<FormMessage>`.
- **Section headings inside forms** (`<h3>`) use
  `font-display text-base font-semibold tracking-tight` — never blend them
  with input labels (`text-sm font-medium`).

## Common bug pattern — TEMPORAL DEAD ZONE
When you compute a derived value, **declare it BEFORE any useEffect that
references it.** Reading a `const` before its declaration throws
`Cannot access 'X' before initialization` and takes the whole React tree
down (blank page). The `FinancePage` and `ChangeRoomSheet` have hit this
twice — keep new code declaring first, using second.

## Verification before "done"
1. `node node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --noEmit` → no errors
2. `node node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js build` → clean
3. **Playwright headless render of the affected route** → no `pageerror`,
   root has content. HTTP 200 alone is NOT enough.
4. If it's a CRUD flow, click through the primary happy path.

## Useful commands
```bash
# type-check only
npx tsc --noEmit

# production build
npx vite build

# git: always feature branch
git checkout -b feature/<short-name>
git add -A
git commit -m "feat(scope): summary"
git push -u origin feature/<short-name>
```

When the user reports a blank page, default to:
1. Spin up the dev server (`npx vite --port 5182 --host 0.0.0.0`)
2. Use Playwright headless to navigate to the affected route
3. Listen for `page.on('pageerror', ...)` — almost always reveals the cause

## Mock data
- All data in `src/lib/mock/data.ts`. State in `src/stores/dataStore.ts`.
- Three hostels: A, C, D (all at "G-12 near SLS School").
- Nomad codes `NOM-####`. Guests have no fixed codes.
- Independent guest = walk-in, self-pay. Linked guest = assigned to a nomad
  (nomad is financially responsible).

